  "chitchat": [
    "\"Re-rack your weights. It's on the board. It's the first thing on the board.\"",
    "He clicks the stopwatch, looks at it, and clicks it again without saying what he was timing.",
    "\"Strong is easy. Strong for long is the work.\"",
    "\"Don't lift angry. Lift tired. You'll find out the difference.\""
  ],
  "description": "A wide, slow-moving man in his sixties with a nose that has been broken in at least two directions and a stopwatch on a bootlace round his neck. He watches everybody in the room at once and says very little to any of them.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "He goes back to watching the room."
    },
    "hands": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Thanks.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Hands are the Pit, behind the Sump. Slagball lot. Wall and a ball and no manners.\" He shrugs. \"I don't teach that. They do.\""
    },
    "ring": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Right.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Sparring nights. Whenever there's enough of you and somebody to stand in your corner.\" He nods at the ropes. \"Rest of the time it's for leaning on.\""
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What can I do here?",
          "next": "train"
        },
        {
          "label": "What's the ring for?",
          "next": "ring"
        },
        {
          "label": "Just looking.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "He looks you over the way a man checks a used car. \"You training, or you lost?\""
    },
    "train": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What about my reflexes?",
          "next": "hands"
        },
        {
          "label": "Fair enough.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Bench is for your arms. Lie on it and lift. Circuit down the end is for your wind: you drill it until the room goes round.\" He taps the stopwatch. \"Neither of them gives you anything for free. You earn it outside and you spend it in here.\""
    }
  },
